@page "/about"
@using PrivatePayDirectory.Core.Models
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About Private Pay";
    // The one page that talks about insurance: explaining why the rest of the site doesn't.
    var lead = Taxonomy.Professions[0];
}

<section class="w-full bg-gradient-to-br from-[#4a7c59] to-[#3d5244] px-4 sm:px-6 py-14 sm:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center text-white">
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight">Care that stays between you and your provider</h1>
        <p class="text-white/80 mt-5 sm:text-lg">
            Private Pay Directory lists independent professionals who work directly with their clients.
            You choose who you see, you agree on the price, and nobody else is part of the conversation.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 space-y-14">

    <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">What does "private pay" mean?</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Private pay simply means you pay your provider directly for the care or service you receive.
            There's no third party deciding whether you qualify, how many sessions you get, or what your
            time together should focus on. That arrangement is decided between you and your provider.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mt-3">
            It started with therapy, where it matters most, but the idea carries over to chiropractic care,
            massage, coaching, and more. Every professional in this directory works this way.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">Why people choose it</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            @foreach (var (icon, title, body) in new[]
            {
                ("lock", "Your privacy",
                 "What you share stays with you and your provider. Your records aren't sent elsewhere to justify your care."),
                ("flag", "Your goals set the agenda",
                 "You don't need a diagnosis or a qualifying reason to get help. You and your provider decide what to work on."),
                ("all_inclusive", "No arbitrary limits",
                 "Care continues for as long as it's helping, not until an outside rule says the number of sessions is up."),
                ("receipt_long", "Clear, upfront pricing",
                 "You know what a session costs before you book. No surprise bills weeks later."),
                ("schedule", "More time for you",
                 "Providers spend less time on paperwork and more time with their clients, and it shows in the care."),
                ("handshake", "A provider you choose",
                 "Pick the person who fits you, based on their approach, specialties and experience, not on a list someone else gave you."),
            })
            {
                <div class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm p-5 flex gap-4">
                    <span class="flex-shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center h-10 w-10 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary">
                        <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-xl">@icon</span>
                    </span>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">@title</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1 leading-relaxed">@body</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            }
        </div>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Is it affordable?</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Often more than people expect. Many providers here offer a sliding scale based on income, a free
            first consultation so you can see whether it's a good fit, or accept HSA/FSA cards for eligible care.
            Look for these under <strong>Fees &amp; Payment</strong> on a provider's profile, and ask them about
            pricing directly. Good providers are happy to talk about it.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
            @foreach (var (question, answer) in new[]
            {
                ("Why don't you list insurance information?",
                 "Because every provider in this directory is private pay, and the directory is built for people who've chosen that route. "
                 + "Insurance involves sharing your information with a third party, meeting its definition of what's necessary, and living with "
                 + "its limits. Private pay avoids all of that. If you do have out-of-network benefits, some providers can give you a detailed "
                 + "receipt to submit yourself. Ask them directly."),
                ("How do I contact a provider?",
                 "Each profile lists the provider's own phone number, email or website. You contact and book with them directly. "
                 + "We don't handle appointments or payments."),
                ("Are providers checked before they're listed?",
                 "Every profile is reviewed by our team before it appears in the directory. Licensing and certification requirements "
                 + "differ by profession and by state, so ask any provider about their credentials before you begin."),
                ("What happens at the first appointment?",
                 "It's mostly about getting to know each other. Expect your provider to ask what brings you in, a bit of background, "
                 + "what you've already tried, and what you'd like to be different. First sessions often run a little longer than later ones."),
                ("How many sessions will I need?",
                 "It depends on what you're working on. Your provider should suggest a rough plan early on, check in with you regularly "
                 + "about how it's going, and talk openly with you about when you're ready to finish. Some focused goals take only a handful "
                 + "of sessions; other work takes longer. Either way, it's your decision, not a preset limit."),
                ("What if a provider isn't the right fit?",
                 "That's normal, and worth saying. A good provider will tell you if someone else would serve you better and help you "
                 + "find them, and you're always free to look for someone new in the directory."),
                ("Can I use an HSA or FSA?",
                 "Often, yes, for eligible care such as therapy or chiropractic. Check with your plan administrator, and look for "
                 + "\"HSA/FSA Accepted\" on a provider's profile."),
                ("I'm a provider. How do I get listed?",
                 "Create an account and choose \"Join as Provider\". Once your profile is reviewed and approved, it appears in your profession's directory."),
            })
            {
                <details class="group bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
                    <summary class="list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 font-semibold text-slate-900">
                        @question
                        <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-slate-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">expand_more</span>
                    </summary>
                    <p class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">@answer</p>
                </details>
            }
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="text-center">
        <a asp-page="/Directory" asp-route-slug="@lead.Slug"
           class="inline-block px-8 py-4 bg-primary text-white font-semibold rounded-xl shadow hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors">
            Browse @lead.PluralName
        </a>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500">
            or <a asp-page="/Index" class="text-primary hover:underline">see every kind of provider</a>
        </p>
    </section>
</div>
